# LeakSanitizer suppressions (LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<this file>).
# Format: one `leak:<substring of a frame's function / module / file>` per line.
#
# Rules for adding an entry:
#   * Third-party or platform noise only. A leak in first-party code is a bug: fix it.
#   * One line of justification above each entry (what leaks, why we can't fix it,
#     upstream issue link if any) so entries can be pruned when the dependency moves on.
#
# Known-benign, deliberately empty until the first real sanitizer run produces a
# report that is proven to originate in a dependency.
#
# Typical candidates (NOT enabled; uncomment only with a matching report in hand):
#   Fontconfig singletons living for the process lifetime:
#   leak:libfontconfig
#   Mesa / driver state created by the offscreen QPA GL probe:
#   leak:libGLX_mesa
#   leak:libEGL_mesa
